  "coverage": [
    "Guarded same-variant enum Tail phases reuse the maintained numeric phase, current-array version proof, source CFG, finite schedule, first-change owner bridge and Cranelift scalar/array emission.",
    "A pure compiler projection retains the original disjoint physical tag/payload layout. Runtime checks the current entry tag; every native backedge independently proves the same tag and exact array roots. Matching schemas alone grant no identity or freshness.",
    "The original selected EnumPack factory certifies the exact constant ordinal and identity payload axes. Invocation entry checks the full logical enum/payload output envelope as well as actual typed array views.",
    "All seven exact scalar kinds, independent row/column checks, immutable aliases, first-change/no-op stores, exact signed-zero/NaN payload bits, older-version rejection and original source error positions are checked in original/decoded/restored execution with Object emission.",
    "Cold exits finish the synchronous loan before unsupported source actions. They export exact current scalar and owner homes, clear inactive variants and publish the valid tag last.",
    "Ordinary different-tag construction rearms a fresh eligible-state preview. A refused hot run remembers refusal, avoiding per-iteration retries until a different variant is constructed. Both paths have observed execution tests.",
    "The represented variant is selected by static numeric operation count, with schema-order ties. No program name, benchmark timing or holdout observation selects it.",
    "Five new tagged-state tests include eight finite dimensions, output preservation, recovery/retry, aliases, exact source errors, observable older array versions and actual native execution without per-iteration library dispatch."
  ],
